BT 1 0 0 1 0 109.2000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (This lecture explores how a growth mindset can be developed through practice and changes in the) Tj T* (way a person responds to effort, challenges and setbacks. A growth mindset is based on the idea) Tj T* (that abilities can improve over time. It encourages learners to focus on progress rather than treating) Tj T* (their present level of performance as a permanent limit. Improvement is a process, so it usually) Tj T* (requires repeated attempts and a willingness to learn from experience. One practical step is to) Tj T* (replace fixed statements with learning-focused statements. Instead of saying \223I cannot understand) Tj T* (this,\224 a learner can say \223I do not understand this yet, so I need to identify the part that is confusing) Tj T* (me.\224 This change does not remove the difficulty, but it makes the next action clearer. Another) Tj T* (important step is to set specific goals. A goal such as \223improve programming\224 is broad, whereas) Tj T* ET
