BT 1 0 0 1 0 201.6000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Building on the importance of time awareness, this lecture focuses on using available hours) Tj T* (efficiently. Effective time use begins with clear priorities. Not every task has the same importance or) Tj T* (urgency, so a learner should decide which activities need attention first. A short priority list can) Tj T* (prevent minor tasks from taking up the time needed for important academic work. Planning also) Tj T* (requires realistic estimates. If a task is expected to take twenty minutes but usually takes an hour,) Tj T* (the schedule will repeatedly become difficult to follow. Estimating duration from previous experience) Tj T* (can make plans more practical. It is also helpful to divide large assignments into smaller steps.) Tj T* (Completing a defined step gives a clearer sense of progress and makes it easier to resume work) Tj T* (later. Efficiency does not mean rushing or attempting several demanding tasks at once. Constantly) Tj T* (switching between activities can interrupt concentration. Working on one priority for a focused) Tj T* (period, taking a suitable break and then reviewing progress may be more effective. A useful plan) Tj T* (should also leave some flexibility for unexpected tasks or delays. For a student, these methods can) Tj T* (be applied to programming practice, assignment preparation and revision. Instead of writing \223study) Tj T* (programming\224 on a list, the task can be divided into actions such as reviewing one concept, solving) Tj T* (an exercise, testing the result and noting a question. At the end of the day, the plan can be reviewed) Tj T* (and adjusted based on what was actually completed.) Tj T* ET
