BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.8000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Assessment decides how students learn, so the choice between AI-based and teacher-based) Tj T* (methods matters in engineering education. Each has clear strengths and weaknesses.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.37008 497.8200 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 56.4000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (In terms of accuracy, AI tools are consistent. An automated system can evaluate hundreds of code) Tj T* (submissions or objective answers using the same rules every time, without getting tired. Teachers,) Tj T* (on the other hand, can understand a student's reasoning in a long derivation or a design report,) Tj T* (which software often misses. Therefore, AI is accurate for objective answers, whereas teachers are) Tj T* (better for open-ended ones.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.37008 439.8200 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 43.2000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Feedback time is where AI wins most clearly. Students receive results and error explanations within) Tj T* (seconds, while manual evaluation of a large class may take weeks. Quick feedback lets students) Tj T* (correct their mistakes while the topic is still fresh. Conversely, a teacher's comments arrive more) Tj T* (slowly but are usually more personal and motivating.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.37008 395.0200 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.0000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Regarding fairness, AI does not show favouritism or mood-based marking. However, it can carry) Tj T* (hidden bias from the data it was trained on, and it may penalise students who give unusual but valid) Tj T* (solutions. A teacher can notice such cases and adjust the marks.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.37008 367.4200 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.8000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Finally, human judgement remains important. Engineering involves creativity, ethics and teamwork,) Tj T* (which cannot be reduced to a score.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
