0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 69.6000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (Modern eco-friendly practices can preserve the core spirit of the festival. Instead of burning plastic) Tj T* (and old tyres on Bhogi, communities can burn only dry leaves or turn them into compost, which) Tj T* (reduces smoke and air pollution. Clay pots, banana leaves and areca-leaf plates can replace plastic) Tj T* (and thermocol, and kolams can be drawn with natural rice flour. Villages can organise tree-planting) Tj T* (drives, rainwater harvesting and cloth-bag campaigns during the festival, and use solar lamps) Tj T* (instead of excess electric decorations.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 85.37008 359.4200 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 16.8000 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 13.2 TL (In this way, Pongal can remain joyful and traditional while staying kind to nature, and the next) Tj T* (generation will learn that celebration and conservation can go together.) Tj T* ET
